[Music]  in kabul the capital of afghanistan life  here is changing rapidly under the new  regime of the taliban now that the  islamic emirate of afghanistan has been  proclaimed and that replaced the afghan  republic that was deposed in the middle  of august already the city is changing  visibly before i rise the  visual transformation is quite striking  the city used to be  covered with graffiti with paintings of  afghan national heroes of women  activists  of historical figures  now a fresh coat of paint is going all  over that  and increasingly the slogans of the  islamic emirate are replacing the  visuals that used to characterize kabul  as you walk around you can see that  merchants are walking between cars  selling big and small flags of islamic  emirate the white flag with the islamic  scripture that has replaced the black  red and green flag of the now deposed  republic of afghanistan  there are protests now every day mostly  led by women that are being dispersed by  the taliban and yet continue the after  day the taliban have proven themselves  to be a highly successful military force  however the fighters don't have much  experience with the peaceful street  protests that we're seeing now they  haven't been trained they don't have  riot equipment and what they do is shoot  in the air sometimes missing and hitting  buildings  the fact that the new government doesn't  include any women says a lot by itself  and so that is the reason why many of  them protesting many of them are down in  the streets saying if this government  stays the way it is if if there is no  transformation that a lot of their  achievements over the last 20 years  at least in the urban areas afghanistan  will be gone forever  while taliban haven't yet spelled out  what rules they will implement many of  the women are preoccupied occupied and  alarmed uh by the fact that they will  probably be able to continue working in  many professions the educational  opportunities will be reduced  the government has has already received  the agreement international criticism  and has not been recognized by anyone  and yet for now it seems to be  in firm control of the city despite  these occasional demonstrations

